<title>USA: NYSE seeks to delist CasTech Aluminum.</title>
<headline>NYSE seeks to delist CasTech Aluminum.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said on Friday it will suspend trading in the common stock of CasTech Aluminum Group Inc and it will seek to delist the company's shares.</p>
<p>Fewer than 600,000 shares remain publicly held after Commonwealth Aluminum Corp's tender offer for the company that expired on September 19, 1996, the exchange said.</p>
<p>The exchange said it may suspend a security if it believes that continued dealings in the security are not advisable.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Aluminum said earlier that 12.7 million shares of CasTech were tendered at $20.50 per share.</p>
</text>
